# Import & Export Conventions

## Use $lib Alias

Always use `$lib` instead of relative paths:

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
import { log, formatZodErrors, MySchema } from '$lib';
import { myService, PrivateEnvValue } from '$lib/server';

// ❌ BAD
import { log } from '../../../utils/logger';
import { myService } from '../../server/services/myService';
```

## Barrel Files

Each module has an `index.ts` that re-exports:

```typescript
// src/lib/schemas/index.ts
export * from './meeting';
export * from './recording';
export * from './myNewSchema';  // Add new schemas here

// src/lib/server/services/index.ts
import * as meetingService from './meeting.service';
import * as recordingService from './recording.service';
export { meetingService, recordingService };
```

## Import Order

1. External packages
2. `$lib` imports
3. `$lib/server` imports (in server files)
4. Relative imports (rare, avoid when possible)

```typescript
// External
import { json, error } from '@sveltejs/kit';
import { RoomsClient } from '@azure/communication-rooms';

// $lib
import { log, formatZodErrors, type Meeting } from '$lib';

// $lib/server
import { meetingService, PrivateEnvValue } from '$lib/server';
```

## Type Imports

Use `type` keyword for type-only imports:

```typescript
import { log, type Meeting, type StoredRecording } from '$lib';
```
